.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The file is as strong as the passphrase: Argon2id makes each guess cost
.Fa m
KiB of memory and
.Fa t
passes, but a short or common passphrase is still found.
The defaults (64 MiB, 3 passes, 4 lanes) are the second recommended
option of RFC 9106 section 4; raise
.Fa m
where the machines that open the file allow it.
.Pp
The parameters and the salt are in the clear, and the length of the
secret key shows its algorithm.
The passphrase is not wiped by these functions; the caller wipes it with
.Xr nqwipe 3 .
